# Supabase Configuration for Mentors Studio Admin Panel
# ----------------------------------------------------
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Run the SQL schema script in supabase/schema.sql in your Supabase SQL Editor
# 3. Copy your project URL and public anon key from Project Settings -> API
# 4. Copy this file to .env and fill in the values below:

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTE:
# Do NOT place the Supabase 'service_role' secret key in this file or any frontend code!
# The Vite frontend only uses the public anon key. All write restrictions and admin checks
# are strictly enforced by Postgres Row Level Security (RLS) policies on the database.
# The service-role key bypasses RLS and must NEVER be exposed to the browser or committed to git.

